\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do I get there from Takuapa town centre?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Head to Takuapa Old Town, then take Thanon Klan Kaew or Soi Khiri Khet\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the history of this place?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"It was originally a forest-dwelling monks' retreat and is around 200 years old. Locals call it Wat Lum because it stands on low-lying ground\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is there to see?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"An ancient chedi base with a large banyan tree growing on it. Municipal information identifies it as an important focus of community faith, located within the temple\"}}]}]",
